ng out after work.","퇴근 후 같이 놀았어요."],["recommend","v","추천하다","A2","Can you recommend a restaurant?","식당 추천해 주실래요?"],["hobby","n","취미","A1","What are your hobbies?","취미가 뭐예요?"],["get into","phr","~에 빠지다","B1","I've gotten into running.","요즘 달리기에 빠졌어요."],["look forward to","phr","기대하다","A2","I look forward to the trip.","여행이 기대돼요."],["by the way","phr","그런데","A2","By the way, congrats on the launch!","그런데 출시 축하해요!"],["congratulations","n","축하","A2","Congratulations on your promotion!","승진 축하해요!"],["exhausted","adj","몹시 지친","B1","I'm exhausted after the flight.","비행 후 너무 지쳤어요."],["jet lag","n","시차증","B1","Are you still jet-lagged?","아직 시차 적응 중이세요?"],["weather","n","날씨","A1","The weather is lovely today.","오늘 날씨 좋네요."],["humid","adj","습한","B1","Seoul is so humid in July.","7월 서울은 정말 습해요."],["chilly","adj","쌀쌀한","B1","It's a bit chilly today.","오늘 좀 쌀쌀하네요."],["traffic","n","교통 체증","A2","Sorry, traffic was terrible.","죄송해요, 차가 엄청 막혔어요."],["holiday","n","휴일, 휴가","A2","Any plans for the holiday?","연휴 계획 있으세요?"],["vacation","n","휴가","A2","I just got back from vacation.","휴가에서 막 돌아왔어요."],["neighborhood","n","동네","B1","I live in a quiet neighborhood.","조용한 동네에 살아요."],["grab a bite","phr","간단히 먹다","B1","Want to grab a bite?","간단히 뭐 먹을래요?"],["treat","v/n","대접하다; 한턱","B1","Lunch is my treat.","점심은 제가 살게요."],["sounds good","phr","좋아요","A2","Sounds good to me.","저는 좋아요."],["no worries","phr","괜찮아요","A2","No worries at all.","전혀 괜찮아요."],["small world","phr","세상 참 좁다","B1","You know him? Small world!","그분 아세요? 세상 좁네요!"],["ice breaker","n","분위기를 푸는 말","B2","That was a great ice breaker.","분위기 푸는 데 딱이었어요."],["by any chance","phr","혹시","B1","Are you from Busan, by any chance?","혹시 부산 출신이세요?"],["awkward","adj","어색한","B1","Sorry, that was awkward.","죄송해요, 좀 어색했네요."],["recharge","v","재충전하다","B1","I need a weekend to recharge.","재충전할 주말이 필요해요."]]},{"id":"travel","sit":"daily/life","name":"출장 · 여행 · 생활","icon":"✈️","desc":"공항·호텔·식당·교통에서 막히지 않는 단어","words":[["itinerary","n","여행 일정표","B2","I sent you the itinerary.","일정표 보내드렸어요."],["boarding pass","n","탑승권","A2","Here is my boarding pass.","탑승권 여기 있어요."],["layover","n","경유 대기","B1","I have a three-hour layover.","경유 대기가 3시간이에요."],["aisle seat","n","통로 좌석","A2","Could I have an aisle seat?","통로 좌석으로 주시겠어요?"],["carry-on","n","기내 반입 가방","B1","Is this carry-on okay?","이거 기내 반입돼요?"],["baggage claim","n","수하물 찾는 곳","A2","Where is baggage claim?","수하물 찾는 곳이 어디예요?"],["customs","n","세관","B1","I have nothing to declare at customs.","세관에 신고할 건 없어요."],["delay","n/v","지연(되다)","A2","My flight is delayed.","비행기가 지연됐어요."],["reservation","n","예약","A2","I have a reservation under Kim.","김으로 예약했어요."],["check in","phr","체크인하다","A2","I'd like to check in.","체크인하려고요."],["check out","phr","체크아웃하다","A2","What time is check-out?","체크아웃은 몇 시예요?"],["amenities","n","편의 시설","B2","What amenities are included?","어떤 편의 시설이 포함돼요?"],["receipt","n","영수증","A2","Could I get a receipt?","영수증 주시겠어요?"],["expense","n","경비","B1","I'll put it on my expense report.","경비 보고서에 올릴게요."],["reimburse","v","비용을 돌려주다","B2","The company will reimburse me.","회사가 비용을 돌려줄 거예요."],["split the bill","phr","나눠 내다","B1","Let's split the bill.","나눠서 내요."],["tip","n","팁","A2","Is tip included?","팁 포함인가요?"],["allergic","adj","알레르기가 있는","B1","I'm allergic to peanuts.","땅콩 알레르기가 있어요."],["vegetarian","adj","채식의","B1","Do you have vegetarian options?","채식 메뉴 있어요?"],["directions","n","길 안내","A2","Could you give me directions?","길 좀 알려주시겠어요?"],["walking distance","n","걸어갈 거리","B1","It's within walking distance.","걸어갈 만한 거리예요."],["fare","n","요금(교통)","B1","What's the taxi fare?","택시 요금이 얼마예요?"],["platform","n","승강장","A2","Which platform for Busan?","부산행은 몇 번 승강장이에요?"],["round trip","n","왕복","A2","A round-trip ticket, please.","왕복표 주세요."],["book","v","예약하다","A2","I'll book a table for four.","4명 자리 예약할게요."],["upgrade","n/v","업그레이드(하다)","B1","Any chance of an upgrade?","업그레이드 가능할까요?"],["lost and found","n","분실물 보관소","B1","Where is the lost and found?","분실물 보관소가 어디예요?"],["local","adj","현지의","A2","What do locals eat here?","현지인은 여기서 뭘 먹어요?"],["jet-lagged","adj","시차로 피곤한","B1","I'm still jet-lagged.","아직 시차 때문에 피곤해요."],["sightseeing","n","관광","B1","Any time for sightseeing?","관광할 시간 있으세요?"]]},{"id":"nuance","sit":"meeting/discussion","name":"뉘앙스 · 완곡 · 의견","icon":"🎚","desc":"세게도, 부드럽게도 — 톤을 고르는 단어","words":[["slightly","adv","약간","B1","It's slightly over budget.","예산을 약간 넘어요."],["somewhat","adv","다소","B2","The results were somewhat mixed.","결과가 다소 엇갈렸어요."],["fairly","adv","꽤, 상당히","B1","I'm fairly confident.","꽤 자신 있어요."],["quite","adv","꽤","A2","That's quite expensive.","꽤 비싸네요."],["relatively","adv","상대적으로","B2","It's relatively simple.","상대적으로 간단해요."],["arguably","adv","거의 틀림없이","C1","It's arguably the best option.","아마 최선의 안일 거예요."],["presumably","adv","아마","C1","Presumably, they will renew.","아마 갱신하겠죠."],["apparently","adv","듣자 하니","B1","Apparently, the CFO left.","듣자 하니 CFO가 떠났대요."],["frankly","adv","솔직히","B2","Frankly, the price is too high.","솔직히 가격이 너무 높아요."],["admittedly","adv","인정하건대","C1","Admittedly, we made a mistake.","인정하건대 저희 실수였어요."],["ideally","adv","이상적으로는","B2","Ideally, we launch in May.","이상적으로는 5월 출시예요."],["potentially","adv","잠재적으로","B2","This could potentially save money.","이게 잠재적으로 비용을 줄일 수 있어요."],["tend to","phr","~하는 경향이 있다","B1","Customers tend to wait until Q4.","고객들은 4분기까지 기다리는 경향이 있어요."],["I would argue","phr","제 생각엔 ~라고 봅니다","B2","I would argue it is worth it.","그럴 가치가 있다고 봐요."],["it seems","phr","~인 것 같다","A2","It seems the issue is fixed.","문제가 해결된 것 같아요."],["not necessarily","phr","꼭 그렇진 않다","B2","Cheaper is not necessarily better.","싸다고 꼭 좋은 건 아니에요."],["to some extent","phr","어느 정도","B2","I agree to some extent.","어느 정도는 동의해요."],["on the other hand","phr","반면에","B1","On the other hand, it is slower.","반면에 더 느려요."],["having said that","phr","그렇긴 해도","B2","Having said that, we can try.","그렇긴 해도 해볼 수는 있어요."],["fair enough","phr","일리 있네요","B1","Fair enough, let us revisit.","일리 있네요, 다시 보죠."],["point taken","phr","말씀 알겠어요","B2","Point taken, we will adjust.","말씀 알겠습니다, 조정할게요."],["I see where you are coming from","phr","무슨 말씀인지 알겠어요","B2","I see where you are coming from.","어떤 취지인지 이해해요."],["reluctant","adj","내키지 않는","B2","They are reluctant to switch.","그들은 전환을 꺼려요."],["hesitant","adj","망설이는","B2","The client is hesitant.","고객이 망설여요."],["keen","adj","열의가 있는","B2","We're keen to move forward.","진행하고 싶어요."],["skeptical","adj","회의적인","B2","I'm a bit skeptical.","조금 회의적이에요."],["confident","adj","자신 있는","A2","We're confident in the plan.","계획에 자신 있어요."],["concerned","adj","걱정하는","B1","I'm concerned about security.","보안이 걱정돼요."],["optimistic","adj","낙관적인","B1","I'm optimistic about Q4.","4분기는 낙관적이에요."],["critical","adj","중대한; 비판적인","B1","This step is critical.","이 단계가 중요해요."]]},{"id":"phrasal","sit":"meeting/discussion","name":"구동사 · 관용 표현","icon":"🧩","desc":"원어민이 입에 달고 사는 덩어리","words":[["bring up","phr","(화제를) 꺼내다","B1","I'd like to bring up the budget.","예산 얘기를 꺼내고 싶어요."],["run by","phr","(의견을) 물어보다","B2","Let me run this by my boss.","상사에게 먼저 확인해 볼게요."],["go ahead","phr","진행하다","A2","Please go ahead.","진행하세요."],["hold off","phr","보류하다","B2","Let's hold off on the purchase.","구매는 보류하죠."],["back up","phr","뒷받침하다","B1","Can you back that up with data?","데이터로 뒷받침할 수 있나요?"],["cut back","phr","줄이다","B1","We need to cut back on costs.","비용을 줄여야 해요."],["fall through","phr","무산되다","B2","The deal fell through.","딜이 무산됐어요."],["pull off","phr","해내다","B2","We pulled it off.","해냈어요."],["step in","phr","나서다, 개입하다","B2","Our CTO stepped in.","CTO가 나섰어요."],["hand over","phr","넘겨주다","B1","I'll hand over the account.","계정을 인계할게요."],["take over","phr","인수하다","B1","Who will take over this project?","이 프로젝트는 누가 맡나요?"],["work out","phr","잘 풀리다; 해결하다","B1","Hopefully it will work out.","잘 풀리면 좋겠어요."],["narrow down","phr","좁히다","B2","Let's narrow down the options.","선택지를 좁히죠."],["iron out","phr","(문제를) 해결하다","C1","We need to iron out the details.","세부 사항을 정리해야 해요."],["get the ball rolling","phr","일을 시작하다","B2","Let's get the ball rolling.","시작해 보죠."],["on the same page","phr","같은 이해를 가진","B2","Are we on the same page?","같은 이해인가요?"],["low-hanging fruit","phr","쉽게 얻는 성과","C1","Start with the low-hanging fruit.","쉬운 것부터 하세요."],["move the needle","phr","의미 있는 변화를 만들다","C1","This will move the needle.","이게 판을 바꿀 거예요."],["in the loop","phr","계속 공유받는","B2","Keep me in the loop.","계속 공유해 주세요."],["up in the air","phr","미정인","B2","The date is still up in the air.","날짜는 아직 미정이에요."],["on the fence","phr","결정 못 한","B2","They're still on the fence.","아직 결정을 못 했어요."],["hit the ground running","phr","즉시 성과를 내다","C1","I can hit the ground running.","바로 성과를 낼 수 있어요."],["think outside the box","phr","창의적으로 생각하다","B2","We need to think outside the box.","틀을 벗어나 생각해야 해요."],["the big picture","phr","전체 그림","B2","Let's look at the big picture.","큰 그림을 보죠."],["a no-brainer","phr","고민할 필요 없는 일","B2","It's a no-brainer.","고민할 필요도 없어요."],["ballpark figure","phr","대략적인 수치","B2","Just a ballpark figure is fine.","대략적인 수치면 돼요."],["cut corners","phr","대충 하다","B2","We don't cut corners.","저희는 대충 하지 않아요."],["touch on","phr","간단히 언급하다","B2","I'll touch on pricing later.","가격은 나중에 간단히 다룰게요."],["follow up on","phr","후속 조치하다","B1","I'll follow up on that.","그건 후속으로 챙길게요."],["reach out","phr","연락하다","B1","Feel free to reach out.","편하게 연락 주세요."]]}]}